  "job": "Cuts lines of glass through the back line and is gone before anyone can answer.",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "lore": "Rishal carried messages between the spires of the Glass Belfry until he got bored of stairs. Now he runs the long way across the dial, and wherever his feet strike the stone a thin road of dawnglass sets behind him. Aubade engineers have asked him to slow down so they can study it. He has not. He talks fast, decides faster and treats every fight as a race he is already winning. His two glass knives are older than he is; he says they were a gift, and changes the story each time.",
